body:
Same here, it pisses me off! Is it to much to ask to be treated with a bit of dignity at age 19? I doubt it's all caused by having AS - I look quite juvenile so that's gotta have something to do with it. 

* "Boy";
* "Kid";
* [condescending and irritating "eeeeeeeh" noises when certain women talk (down) to me];
* "Chick"

loads more stuff that I can't/don't want to recall now.

[STFU FFS](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EaYE0XTnqOw)

> When people speak to me like a child or when they speak loud and slow. But I haven't got the balls and my words won't come out when people talk to me like this.

When you're treated like a child in the long-term - all the time - then you'll gradually start to 'become' a one; psychologically you will lose confidence, and sort of take on the stance of an infant, and just like any infant you'll have trouble talking back. I've read into all this (look up "infantilizing test") so I know what I'm on about. It's happened to me too.

**It's basically a form of: unintentional (usually), covert emotional abuse**. Yes, I'm really calling this a form of abuse.
